    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="0805" n="1313" xml:id="pg1313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Truman Papers, President’s Secretary’s File</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Truman to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">personal and confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-08-16">August 16, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I read the memorandum<anchor n="1" xml:id="d530-f1"/> regarding the Israel
                    request for $100 million loan and I sincerely hope that there will not be a flat
                    turndown until further consideration has been given by the World Bank.</p>
                <p>Of course, I don’t want any loans made that are not proper for the Bank to make
                    but this situation has all sorts of implications.</p>
                <p>Sometime in the not too far distant future I’d like to have a conversation with
                    you on the subject and incidentally on several other subjects about which I do
                    not want to talk with the Secretary because of their political implications.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">arry</hi>] S. T[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ruman</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
